## Part One: User Agreement

### I. Scope of Agreement

Welcome to Simple record (hereinafter referred to as the "Application"). This Agreement sets out the rights and obligations between you and the above-mentioned operating entity (hereinafter referred to as "we," "us," or "our") regarding your use of the Application. Part Two of this document, the Privacy Policy and Permissions Description, explains the rules for processing personal information and should be read together with this Agreement.

The Application obtains your confirmation of this Agreement through the corresponding confirmation action; authorization involving personal information processing, provision of data to third-party AI, and device permissions shall be obtained separately in accordance with applicable laws and the prompts for specific functions, and your reading of this Agreement cannot replace the necessary explicit consent.

### II. Service Content

The Application provides functions such as text Q&A, image-assisted understanding, voice recognition input, chat history, text favorites, and note management. You can edit notes and send text to an application of your choice through the system sharing function.

AI Q&A and image understanding rely on the third-party DeepSeek service. Voice input uses Apple speech recognition: after recording is transcribed, you can review and modify the text before sending it to the AI. The current version does not send original recordings as audio input directly to DeepSeek.

Saved chat records, images, and recordings, as well as favorited text and notes, can be viewed on the corresponding pages. Favorites and notes are saved independently of the original chat; deleting the original chat will not automatically delete these copies.

The service may be affected by network conditions, device capabilities, system permissions, third-party service availability, and usage quotas. The scope of functions and quotas shall be subject to the descriptions on the actual, clear product pages; if paid services are introduced in the future, the price, service term, and cancellation method will be separately explained before purchase.

### III. Account and Device Use

If the Application requires registration or login, please provide lawful and necessary account information and properly safeguard your password and login credentials. If you discover that your account has been misappropriated, please contact us promptly. We will not ask you to provide your full password through feedback channels.

Some materials in the Application are stored locally on the device. Changing devices, uninstalling the Application, clearing data, or device failure may result in the inability to recover local materials; system backup and recovery are determined by the system services you use. The Application currently does not promise note cloud synchronization or cross-device recovery services. Please use methods such as sharing to retain copies of important text yourself.

### IV. Usage Rules

