## Part Two: Privacy Policy and Permissions Description

### I. Scope of Application and Important Notes

This Policy explains how Simple record (hereinafter referred to as the "Application") processes information and uses system permissions when providing AI chat, image understanding, voice input, chat history, text favorites, notes, and related account services.

**Content sent to AI will leave your device.** The current client uses DeepSeek to provide text Q&A and image understanding; voice recognition uses Apple system services and may require sending recordings to Apple servers.

**Chat records, images, recordings, favorites, and notes are stored locally on the device.** The Application is not a "zero-storage" service. Deleting local content does not mean that content previously processed or retained by third parties in accordance with law has been deleted.

This Policy does not replace functional prompts, explicit consent, or system permission authorization that need to be displayed separately. If the purpose, method, or scope of personal information processing changes and reauthorization is required by law, separate notice shall be given and corresponding consent shall be obtained.

### II. What Information Is Processed for Different Functions

#### 1. Account and Basic Services

If you use registration, login, or profile modification functions, the relevant services will process information you fill in, such as account name, password, nickname, and avatar, and may also process account identifiers, login credentials, device model, system or application version, etc., to complete identity verification, profile display, and service operation.

The deployment region, specific log fields, and retention period of the server are [To be completed: verify according to the actual configuration of the account and basic service backend]. Please do not list information that you do not actually collect as required information; if other login methods or authentication functions are actually provided, corresponding data explanations should be supplemented.

#### 2. Text Q&A and Image Understanding

When you confirm sending a message, the client will send the current text and historical text used for context understanding in the current session to DeepSeek. If the current session contains sent images, these images may also be submitted together in subsequent follow-up questions.

Images you select or take will generate an image copy suitable for sending on the device. The image itself and visible text, portraits, and other content in it will be processed by DeepSeek to generate a reply. Selecting or previewing an image does not equal sending it to DeepSeek; actual submission occurs after you confirm sending.

The server and network service providers may receive necessary network connection information, such as IP address, when processing requests. For third-party information, see Part IV. Please check the input content and avoid submitting sensitive information unrelated to the question.

#### 3. Voice Recording and Recognition

When you actively use voice input, we request microphone and speech recognition permissions, record the voice you actively input, and generate text through Apple speech recognition services.

Depending on the device, language, and system service support, recognition may require handing the recording to Apple servers for processing, and it cannot be guaranteed that it will always be completed only on the device. You can review and modify the recognized text before confirming sending. **What is sent to DeepSeek is the confirmed text, not the original recording file.**

Recordings that are completed and sent are retained locally for voice message playback. When canceling a recording or removing an unsent voice attachment, the Application will clean up the corresponding local file; abnormal exit may leave temporary files.

#### 4. Chat History, Favorites, and Notes

Chat text, AI replies, and related images and recordings are stored in the Application's local storage for viewing and continuing conversations. When continuing a conversation, the relevant context may be sent to DeepSeek again.

Text you actively favorite and notes you create or edit are saved locally; the saving and search operations themselves will not automatically submit favorites or notes to DeepSeek. Favorites and notes are stored separately according to in-app account information; this arrangement is not equivalent to end-to-end encryption, nor does it mean that all chat history on the same device has been isolated by account.

Favorites and notes are independent copies. After deleting the original chat, you still need to separately delete the corresponding content in "Favorite Records" or "My Notes."

#### 5. Copying, Sharing, and Feedback

When you click copy, the selected text is written to the system clipboard. When you actively paste through the system menu, the corresponding text enters the input box; before confirmation of sending, it will not be submitted to DeepSeek merely because of the paste operation.

When you choose "Share Text," the corresponding content will be handed to the application or recipient you choose through the system sharing panel; subsequent processing is also subject to the rules of that application or recipient.

If you use functions such as opinion feedback or customer service contact, we will process the problem description and contact information you actively provide to handle your request. The relevant recipients and backend retention period are [To be completed].

#### 6. Notifications and Other Functions Actually Provided

The project includes implementation related to system push registration. If the actually released version uses push notifications, it should explain the data processing of device push identifiers, notification content, business servers, and Apple Push Notification service, and the specific scope and retention period are [To be completed].

If the final version provides functions such as user-to-user chat, friends, groups, voice calls, or real-name authentication, it is also necessary to supplement their information collection, recipients, content governance, retention, and deletion rules. The AI function explanations in this draft cannot replace complete disclosure for these functions.

### III. System Permission Description

| Permission or Capability | When Used and Purpose | Impact After Refusal or Closure |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Camera | When actively choosing to take a photo, used to take the image to be sent; also used for this purpose when avatar photography is actually provided | Cannot take photos, but text input and available gallery selection methods can still be used |
| Microphone | When actively recording voice, used to collect recordings | Cannot record voice, does not affect text input |
| Speech Recognition | When actively using voice input, used to convert recordings into text | The current voice transcription process is unavailable, does not affect text input |
| System Photo Picker | AI gallery selection uses the system photo picker and only receives images you select | Canceling selection will not add images; this method usually does not require full gallery read permission |
| Photo Read | Applied only when other provided functions that actually need to read the gallery are used | Affects the corresponding gallery function, and text functions should not be blocked because of this |
| Add Photo to Gallery | Applied only when a function to save images to the album is actually provided and used | Cannot save images to the system album |
| Notifications | When message reminders and other functions are actually enabled, the system manages notification permission | Relevant system reminders will no longer be displayed; available functions can still be used when opening the Application |
| Network Access | Login, AI Q&A, image understanding, and voice recognition that may require networking | Cannot complete the corresponding online functions; saved local notes can still be viewed and edited |

You can manage camera, microphone, speech recognition, photos, and other authorizations in iOS "Settings" by entering the Application or "Privacy & Security"; notification permission is managed in system notification settings, and the specific path depends on the system version.

The current AI chat, favorites, and notes do not require device contacts or precise location permissions. Before release, verify whether the entire application has these functions elsewhere, clean up permission declarations with no actual use, or supplement the real purposes; relevant data cannot be considered to have been used by the function merely based on permission declarations.

